<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:32:default:windows">
<!--
    evalcurrentproto: evaluate a function's OWN unknown prototype with the model
    the compiler spec nominates, so register-passed parameters are recovered.

    x86win.cspec declares a merged model and nominates it for the current
    function:

        <resolveprototype name="__fastcall/__thiscall/__stdcall"> ... </resolveprototype>
        <eval_current_prototype name="__fastcall/__thiscall/__stdcall"/>

    kuna decoded the union and registered it by name, but never read the
    <eval_current_prototype> element, so every function was evaluated with
    <default_proto> = __stdcall, whose inputs are stack-only.  A __fastcall
    function's ECX/EDX arguments are then not *possible* parameters and the reads
    of them at entry survive as undefined locals - read before ever being
    written, which no C function can do.

    Source (MSVC/clang i386, __fastcall: a in ECX, b in EDX, c on the stack):

        int __fastcall fc(int a, int b, int c) {
            int r = a * 3 + b;
            if (c > 0) r += c;
            return r;
        }

    built `clang -target i386-pc-windows-msvc -O1 -c`, whose body is
        push esi ; mov esi,[esp+8] ; lea ecx,[ecx+ecx*2] ; add ecx,edx
        xor eax,eax ; test esi,esi ; cmovns eax,esi ; add eax,ecx ; pop esi ; ret 4

    Pass 1 (`option evalcurrentproto off`, assert #1): only the stack argument is
    a parameter; ECX and EDX come out as undefined locals carrying their storage
    comment.

    Pass 2 (default, asserts #2/#3): the merged model resolves per function
    against the trials that are actually active, picks __fastcall, and the
    function takes its three arguments.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x401000" readonly="true">
568b7424088d0c4901d131c085f60f49c601c85ec20400
</bytechunk>
<symbol name="fc" space="ram" offset="0x401000"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>lo fu fc</com>
  <com>option evalcurrentproto off</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option evalcurrentproto on</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="EVALCURRENTPROTO #1: off, the __stdcall default model sees only the stack argument" min="1" max="1">int4 fc\(int4 a0\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="EVALCURRENTPROTO #2: off, the ECX argument survives as an undefined local" min="1" max="1">// ecx</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="EVALCURRENTPROTO #3: default, the spec's merged model resolves to __fastcall and recovers all three arguments" min="1" max="1">int4 fc\(int4 a0,int4 a1,int4 a2\)</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
